module

public import CFSG.Quasithin.Chapter16.Section04To05.InnerFamily.OuterReduction.CoverFusion.Reduction

/-!
# The four double-cover fusion branches of 16.4.9

The shared reduction constructs a residual fusion witness from a two-central
quotient residual involution and its conjugator. It derives the center,
constructs the involutory residual lift, determines the actual quotient-kernel
error, and removes it using the earlier I.2.2 order-four inversion theorem.

The intrinsic marked-fusion calculations for G₂(4), M₁₂, J₂, and HS, and their
separation from the exceptional quotients in 16.1.2(2), remain prerequisites.
No unconditional theorem for these four branches is asserted here yet.

Source: Aschbacher–Smith, combined manuscript of 1 March 2004,
proof of 16.4.9(2), printed p.1191.
-/
